# vvaharness/config/__init__.py

The configuration loader. `load` reads the operator-selected profile YAML, fills every missing scalar step setting from the built-in table `_STEP_DEFAULTS`, deep-merges a trusted `config.local.yaml` overlay on top, expands `${ENV:-default}` placeholders under a secret-name policy, refuses an out-of-range `refusal_retries`, and returns the attribute wrapper `Config`. `apply_step1_overlay` layers a per-scan Stage 1 exclusion file (operator-written or the model-written auto overlay) onto `cfg.step1`. The `_STEP_DEFAULTS` table is the middle layer of every `knob(...)` default: profile value, then this table, then the call-site fallback.

Source: `vvaharness/config/__init__.py` (lines 1-1008)
Executor: code
Called from: `vvaharness/orchestrator/entry.py`, `vvaharness/cli/__init__.py`, `vvaharness/api.py`, `vvaharness/manifest.py` (`load`); `vvaharness/orchestrator/scan.py` scan_repo (`apply_step1_overlay` for the auto Stage 1 overlay)

